Dr. Karan Mittal: The similar model was also given by Abraham Maslow. Abraham Maslow was a transpersonal psychologist, and he defined the five human needs. The first is the physical need, that is Routi Kapra Makan. Then were the security needs, in a sense, having a job, a social security.

523
01:00:28.230 --> 01:00:36.579
Dr. Karan Mittal: Love and belonging, self-esteem, and then self-actualization, that we can term as, you know, kind of attaining the best version of yourself, that is.

524
01:00:36.580 --> 01:00:48.749
Dr. Karan Mittal: Probably, in spiritual terms, it could be dharma, moksha, stable mind, whatever. So that's self-actualization. Now, you cannot try to kind of satisfy one need by going to the higher need.

525
01:00:48.810 --> 01:00:51.289
Dr. Karan Mittal: You have to work on this need first.

526
01:00:51.290 --> 01:01:10.610
Dr. Karan Mittal: Then, go to the second and third game. What we do is we try to kind of settle the level 2 and 3 by telling the person to focus on level 1. It's a struggle. Person cannot do that so easily. So first, work on the mind and the materiality. Third will automatically, as a flow, will be realized.

527
01:01:13.270 --> 01:01:17.710
Dr. Karan Mittal: So this is about the Descartes split, like, the Western… Western…

528
01:01:18.070 --> 01:01:26.230
Dr. Karan Mittal: psychology basically operated on the function of the Cartesian dual. We, in philosophy, we call it as the Cartesian dual, where we separate the mind and the body.

529
01:01:26.520 --> 01:01:36.269
Dr. Karan Mittal: Now, seeing it from an Indic lens, Vyashti and Samashti, like, we have… we also have splits, like… like, we can separate the two. What it helps with

530
01:01:36.270 --> 01:01:47.269
Dr. Karan Mittal: It helps us in a better understanding of the two. Like, when we see bodies separately, it gives us modern medicine, it gives us science, it gives us all the Pratakshrahmanas, it gives all the physical laws that exist.

531
01:01:47.270 --> 01:01:54.449
Dr. Karan Mittal: Okay? But what it takes away from us is the holistic view. This is how the mind influences the body, and vice versa.

532
01:01:54.450 --> 01:02:17.380
Dr. Karan Mittal: What we talk about today, about the psychosomatic illnesses, or psychosomatic diseases, like, many diseases today are said to be psychosomatic. Even the modern medicine and psychology are trying to believe… are now kind of believing that, that diseases like IBS is a psychosomatic, where your digestive system, because of the constant stress, starts reacting to the stress, because the intestine and the brain are connected with each other.

533
01:02:17.380 --> 01:02:40.029
Dr. Karan Mittal: So, also, if there is something called a psychosomatic disease, why can't there be something called a psychosomatic wellness? That if your mind is good, your body automatically starts falling. If you're stress-free, automatically the body will start healing itself better. So, the Dakartan split, or the Cartesian Dual, it gives us the Vashti Sadhna, in the sense it helps us understand both in separate ways.

534
01:02:40.030 --> 01:02:46.840
Dr. Karan Mittal: But what it takes away from us is the samashti, or the sum… or the integration of both, and how both function in reality.

535
01:02:46.840 --> 01:02:53.190
Dr. Karan Mittal: Okay? Or how both are interconnected to each other. So when we talk from an Indic lens, we don't see

536
01:02:53.190 --> 01:03:15.820
Dr. Karan Mittal: when a client comes to us, we don't see just the mind, or when, as a doctor, we just don't see the body. If a person is suffering from a chronic disease, it's also essential to see how the mind is working, because the mind is definitely getting affected by the chronic disease, and vice versa. So when we start seeing a person as a whole, in his old totality, like we've probably said, we'll be covering punch kosher, when we start

537
01:03:15.820 --> 01:03:30.229
Dr. Karan Mittal: Seeing the emotions, when you start seeing the thoughts, when you start seeing what's happening at the material level. The amount of interventions we can do, or the amount of help we can offer to the patient or the client, improves, and the results are also faster.

538
01:03:30.230 --> 01:03:31.150
Dr. Karan Mittal: So…

539
01:03:31.550 --> 01:03:47.690
Dr. Karan Mittal: So, seeing in split is essential. We don't discard Western psychology, it has given us tools, but also seeing it as a whole. I say holistic is W-H-O-L-I-S-I-T-C. So, so that's holistic, like, seeing both as a whole is equally important.

540
01:03:49.270 --> 01:04:00.080
Dr. Karan Mittal: And therefore, if we see our Rishi's perspective, our Rishis never separated the shareil and Manas. They saw it together. In fact, the definition of

541
01:04:00.080 --> 01:04:08.039
Dr. Karan Mittal: swastya that's given by Sushrutta, Marshi Sushruta, also has the personna Chikta Atma Indri.

542
01:04:08.040 --> 01:04:27.410
Dr. Karan Mittal: So, when a person has to be defined as a whole, or as healthy, he also needs to have a person, a happy mind, a happy chitra, and also happy senses. The senses also need to be kind of happy in the sense, not too much of deprivation and not too much of indulgence. So, senses also need to operate Hindu.

543
01:04:27.460 --> 01:04:33.079
Dr. Karan Mittal: And that's why our definition of swastya, or swastya, was always being situated in oneself.

544
01:04:33.390 --> 01:04:48.750
Dr. Karan Mittal: being situated in a true nature. And how did we define true nature? Sachitta Ananda. So, if you're not happy, then you're not helped. So, being… so our definition of swastya is swastya, being situated in your true nature. Anything that takes you away from your true nature.

545
01:04:48.800 --> 01:04:59.470
Dr. Karan Mittal: It's not the healthy stick. So, when a client comes to us, whether it's a physical issue, mental issue, emotional issue, etc, we also see how much is the happiness quotient, how much is the

546
01:04:59.470 --> 01:05:22.720
Dr. Karan Mittal: feeling happy on a day-to-day basis, week-to-week basis, month-to-month basis. Of course, because of the chronic disease, constant happiness is not possible, but is he doing anything that makes him happy on a daily basis? Is he doing anything that makes him happy on a weekly basis? Because these small doses of happiness helps him kind of get situated in his true nature, in his true self, and that helps us kind of, you know, retrieve that client back, or

547
01:05:22.720 --> 01:05:34.809
Dr. Karan Mittal: kind of help the client back to move away from this pathology. So most of the times, when we talk about happiness quotient, or Anandai Pusha, or when we give homeworks to the client, one of the homeworks is also make a list

548
01:05:34.810 --> 01:05:39.449
Dr. Karan Mittal: Of things that make you happy. So I'm working with a female in her 40s.

549
01:05:39.450 --> 01:05:58.410
Dr. Karan Mittal: no particular issue as such, but… but not being able to feel happy on a date. Like… like, she's… she… she… when I told her to write things that makes her feel happy, it took her 3 weeks to get with 2 or 3 things, like walking in the garden, and probably playing, you know, gelling with kids, like playing with kids.

550
01:05:58.560 --> 01:06:19.470
Dr. Karan Mittal: That was the… it took us 3 weeks to get to a list that can she do… that she can do to kind of, you know, feel that happiness on a day-to-day basis. So sometimes you have lost our, you know, maybe… maybe you could take this exercise for yourself. What are the things that make you feel happy? Do you have 5, 6, 7, 8, 10 things that you… and also, how much you do these things on a regular basis?

551
01:06:19.510 --> 01:06:36.690
Dr. Karan Mittal: One of the reasons why we have developed exercises in this module is also exercise… individual exercises, and also exercises in pairs, groups, sharing, is one of the traits, or one of the, one of the requirements to become a good counselor is to feel vulnerable.

552
01:06:37.110 --> 01:06:40.290
Dr. Karan Mittal: Or to know how it feels to sit on that side of the chair.

553
01:06:40.510 --> 01:06:56.350
Dr. Karan Mittal: So when you develop these, when you work on your concepts, when you work on your beliefs, when you work on your judgments and issues, you feel that vulnerability. And when you feel that vulnerability, you know how the client opposite will feel. Earlier, two decades ago, psychology was about the psychologist sitting on a pedestal.

554
01:06:57.140 --> 01:07:12.339
Dr. Karan Mittal: And from that pedestal, the psychologist, you know, kind of commanded, you know, that body language, and then writing with a pen on a note. That was… that was the concept of psychologists. But now, eventually, the psychology is more about being at the same resonance with the client.

555
01:07:12.340 --> 01:07:30.289
Dr. Karan Mittal: And also, experiencing what the client experienced. Probably, the client has depression, I have not felt that depression in my life. But I should know how it feels to sit on that side of the chair, share your inner, inner dark secrets, or inner inhibitions, or inner issues. That helps us become more empathetic.

556
01:07:30.860 --> 01:07:48.379
Dr. Karan Mittal: So, so, nowadays, if you see the modern psychological trainings make it compulsory for the trainers or for the evolving therapists to undergo sessions themselves. They make group exercises, pair exercises, triad exercises, fumble study, because they have to work on their judgment also. Suppose if I have a judgment.

557
01:07:48.380 --> 01:07:53.599
Dr. Karan Mittal: That mind is something that can be tamed. Suppose I have a belief that mind can be tamed.

558
01:07:53.600 --> 01:07:59.670
Dr. Karan Mittal: Every counselli that is sitting in front of me, anything he talks about the mind, I'll be operating from that judgment.

559
01:08:00.230 --> 01:08:07.179
Dr. Karan Mittal: This is a small thing, and this is not a big thing. That small thing for me because of my belief system.

560
01:08:07.210 --> 01:08:23.080
Dr. Karan Mittal: But how big is for that client? That vulnerability is lost. So that's why the exercises designed here are to kind of make you understand what that vulnerability is, and also work on your judgments, your beliefs, your ecosystem within. That will help

561
01:08:23.080 --> 01:08:28.960
Dr. Karan Mittal: you become a better. So, next time when you're talking to a counselor of yours, because most of you are spiritual mentors.

562
01:08:29.000 --> 01:08:34.980
Dr. Karan Mittal: When you're making an analysis, you also analyze from what belief system are you operating this analysis on.

563
01:08:35.160 --> 01:08:40.209
Dr. Karan Mittal: Okay, or what… if you're advising a client, what belief system makes you advise the client on that?

564
01:08:40.450 --> 01:08:46.490
Dr. Karan Mittal: That will help you take yourself a level deeper within, as well as a counselor.

565
01:08:48.700 --> 01:09:00.699
Dr. Karan Mittal: So, the split between, like, what we saw as the Cartesian duality, or the split between body and mind, we never saw it in the Indian tradition. In Indian tradition, everything was taken as a whole.

566
01:09:00.790 --> 01:09:05.429
Dr. Karan Mittal: A way they used to see all the… the way the… like, now, suppose the psychologist

567
01:09:05.490 --> 01:09:25.559
Dr. Karan Mittal: Sorry, a client walks into my room, the way they will start seeing from the way he's walking, the way he's sitting, the way he's talking, all these things are analyzed. We never… it's not like, okay, the client just sat over here and now starts speaking. What is your problem? What are the issues? Who are there in the family? It's not like history-taking.

568
01:09:25.710 --> 01:09:41.350
Dr. Karan Mittal: you see the person as a whole, because these things give you an indication of what might be, you know, happening in his life, or in his society, or in his individual, personal issues. So we saw a person as a whole. Now, even if you see

569
01:09:41.560 --> 01:09:44.689
Dr. Karan Mittal: the kosher theory. All the punch koshas

570
01:09:44.689 --> 01:10:02.350
Dr. Karan Mittal: are definitely seen separately, but in a Jiva, we consider them to be one together, and we analyze the thoughts, we analyze the emotions, we analyze the partnership tree, and finally, we also analyze the physical body. And that gives us a clarity of what's happening. So, for an example,

571
01:10:02.500 --> 01:10:16.560
Dr. Karan Mittal: Suppose I'm… I'm… I'm a wife here, and I'm kind of treating a person with hyperacidity. Now, it's easy for me to prescribe sushikaras, or pantocid, or any of these diseases to curb that acidity.

572
01:10:16.560 --> 01:10:23.490
Dr. Karan Mittal: But when I ask the… ask the primary the history of the client, then I'll come to know that he's in a corporate job, probably CEO of some…

573
01:10:23.490 --> 01:10:32.270
Dr. Karan Mittal: particular, particular company. There's lots of politics that's going on. That increases the stress. The stress is now happening in the thoughts that will affect

574
01:10:32.270 --> 01:10:46.049
Dr. Karan Mittal: the emotions that will affect the pranesharina, and finally it will start affecting the share. This is one of the most gross examples of a psychosomatic disease that will take. So, they will analyze, or in the council will analyze from all these

575
01:10:46.050 --> 01:10:49.120
Dr. Karan Mittal: 4 layers. And he will know where to put a stop.

576
01:10:49.160 --> 01:10:52.899
Dr. Karan Mittal: He'll probably tell him a few exercises to work on his thoughts.

577
01:10:53.010 --> 01:11:05.230
Dr. Karan Mittal: He'll give him a few exercises to kind of work on the emotions, a few exercises to work on the pranasheer, like regulating the prana, the habits, the schedule, and finally.

578
01:11:05.600 --> 01:11:12.110
Dr. Karan Mittal: For the time being, we'll give medicines to curb the acidity, and then eventually these things will start taking over the healing of the heart.

579
01:11:12.270 --> 01:11:22.879
Dr. Karan Mittal: So we saw the person as a group. We never saw the person as one independent, faculty, like mine, or the emotions, or the public. So.

580
01:11:22.880 --> 01:11:41.380
Dr. Karan Mittal: As a counselor, you don't split. You start integrating. So next time someone comes to, take sessions or counseling from you, it's not just the problem that we are discussing, we are healing the person. So we discuss a bit of his family life, a bit of his social life, material life, and then see where is the root cause for the problem lie.

581
01:11:42.480 --> 01:11:43.919
Dr. Karan Mittal: Would you like to add something?

582
01:11:43.920 --> 01:11:45.279
GOVINDA Das: To add, yeah, just to add.

583
01:11:45.910 --> 01:11:50.250
GOVINDA Das: You know, there are 3 things, Sharira, Jiwa, and Atma.

584
01:11:51.010 --> 01:11:55.549
GOVINDA Das: Now, the Sharidah is the body made of Pancha Mahabhat.

585
01:11:55.930 --> 01:11:59.410
GOVINDA Das: earth, water, fire, air, ether. That is called a share.

586
01:12:00.990 --> 01:12:06.540
GOVINDA Das: And then Jiva is what… Jeeva is basically the body.

587
01:12:07.050 --> 01:12:11.330
GOVINDA Das: earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intelligence, and ego.

588
01:12:13.150 --> 01:12:17.179
GOVINDA Das: Including the Atma, that is called as Jiva.

589
01:12:17.870 --> 01:12:21.870
GOVINDA Das: Very important to understand. See, our… our rishis.

590
01:12:22.270 --> 01:12:29.120
GOVINDA Das: They had a brilliant way of explaining. While they would explain, therefore they defined Sankeshastra.

591
01:12:29.320 --> 01:12:33.590
GOVINDA Das: Sankesh Shastra means explaining everything minutely.

592
01:12:34.650 --> 01:12:35.570
GOVINDA Das: Alright?

593
01:12:36.090 --> 01:12:40.319
GOVINDA Das: But that same Sankesh Shastra, while explaining minutely.

594
01:12:40.530 --> 01:12:48.409
GOVINDA Das: the rishis, the Ayurvedic people, or the rishis, They were extremely…

595
01:12:48.590 --> 01:12:52.319
GOVINDA Das: Learn it in regards to integrating the application.

596
01:12:53.870 --> 01:13:00.450
GOVINDA Das: Varanan keile, sang ke hai, application ke liy, samagarata hai.

597
01:13:01.520 --> 01:13:04.840
GOVINDA Das: You know, I need to… I'll translate it, those who don't understand.

598
01:13:05.210 --> 01:13:08.459
GOVINDA Das: Explanation requires Sankhya.

599
01:13:09.540 --> 01:13:12.300
GOVINDA Das: But application requires Samagrata.

600
01:13:12.680 --> 01:13:15.079
GOVINDA Das: No, there is no Kanda Kanda.

601
01:13:15.540 --> 01:13:23.910
GOVINDA Das: Alright, so therefore, again, our, Pancho Kosher. Punchakosh, we will discuss that also.

602
01:13:24.190 --> 01:13:29.780
GOVINDA Das: Generally, the Panchakos is defined, or Anama is the lowest, and Anandma is the highest.

603
01:13:31.250 --> 01:13:38.109
GOVINDA Das: We do not go in hierarchy. That is not step 1, step 2, step 3, step 4, step 5.

604
01:13:38.670 --> 01:13:43.779
GOVINDA Das: The Bharate Kon is always the circular Dhrushti kon, please understand.

605
01:13:46.040 --> 01:13:55.420
GOVINDA Das: It is not… it is not, you know, like a staircase. It is like a, you know, semicircular thing continuously moving.

606
01:13:56.160 --> 01:14:01.790
GOVINDA Das: Till the last breath, one needs to focus on the Annamay Kosh.

607
01:14:01.940 --> 01:14:08.589
GOVINDA Das: In fact, as a man or a woman becomes old, they focus more on their food.

608
01:14:09.720 --> 01:14:19.949
GOVINDA Das: what to eat, what not to eat, how much to eat, how much not to eat. If there is some disturbance in the food, their entire system gets jeopardized.

609
01:14:20.250 --> 01:14:28.459
GOVINDA Das: Right? It is not that because you become spiritually elevated, suddenly you become reckless in regards to your food habits.

610
01:14:29.430 --> 01:14:40.250
GOVINDA Das: So the anamaya remains, and within that Anna Maya, there could be… in that anna only, there could be a prana. In that anna, there could be mano, because who has cooked it?

611
01:14:41.230 --> 01:14:58.720
GOVINDA Das: In that Anna only, there could be Buddhi, Vikyanmay kosher, and that Anna itself, there could be Anandamaya. So every kosher, every aspect has all other aspects in regards to application. Only in regards to explanation, we

612
01:14:58.840 --> 01:15:03.799
GOVINDA Das: do use Sankya. So, therefore, as Karanji was mentioning.

613
01:15:03.910 --> 01:15:11.139
GOVINDA Das: That analysis will always be Sankhya, application will always be yoga.

614
01:15:11.570 --> 01:15:12.860
GOVINDA Das: integrated.

615
01:15:13.500 --> 01:15:14.430
GOVINDA Das: Yeah, next.

616
01:15:15.330 --> 01:15:16.599
Dr. Karan Mittal: And also,

617
01:15:16.720 --> 01:15:28.900
Dr. Karan Mittal: the whole philosophy operates from the Yat Pinde Takra… sorry, Yad Brahmandita Pinde, like, whatever is in the universe kind of starts reflecting into your body. So.

618
01:15:29.070 --> 01:15:43.229
Dr. Karan Mittal: So, when we analyze a person, like, if you even study Ayurveda, Ayurveda starts from… it doesn't start from understanding the body. It starts from understanding the universe and the cosmos first. And then it comes down to understanding the body.

619
01:15:43.230 --> 01:16:01.440
Dr. Karan Mittal: So, if you have… if you kind of skip either of the two, it will start impacting the way you understand the person, or you understand the universe. So, you have to… when you understand the person, you have to understand his universe. In the sense, what I meant to say was you have to start with understanding his universe. That could be things around him.

620
01:16:01.440 --> 01:16:07.410
Dr. Karan Mittal: The emotions, the thoughts, and then finally come to the issue that we're going to address.

621
01:16:07.480 --> 01:16:14.649
Dr. Karan Mittal: In that question. So, before we go ahead, I would like you to kind of just do a small exercise and just close your eyes.

622
01:16:15.710 --> 01:16:21.599
Dr. Karan Mittal: And… and just be as relaxed as possible. We are coming back to the first question that we

623
01:16:21.750 --> 01:16:27.999
Dr. Karan Mittal: Probably started the session with… And I will take that slide later, so that

624
01:16:28.200 --> 01:16:32.509
Dr. Karan Mittal: Yeah, we can just focus on yourself, just focus on your…

625
01:16:32.720 --> 01:16:37.040
Dr. Karan Mittal: Body, or whatever, just close your eyes and just focus on any one thing.

626
01:16:37.180 --> 01:16:43.410
Dr. Karan Mittal: And… just… For a moment, Just see where is your mind?

627
01:16:43.780 --> 01:16:46.600
Dr. Karan Mittal: Where would you localize your mind in the body?

628
01:16:50.430 --> 01:16:52.760
Dr. Karan Mittal: There's no right or wrong as an answer.

629
01:16:54.400 --> 01:17:02.820
Dr. Karan Mittal: Just try to be aware. Where is your mind? Are you able to localize it to a position, a geography, a location?

630
01:17:17.610 --> 01:17:18.490
Dr. Karan Mittal: I agree.

631
01:17:19.300 --> 01:17:23.310
Dr. Karan Mittal: I'll not give too much time to this question, but I want you to kind of now

632
01:17:23.720 --> 01:17:25.530
Dr. Karan Mittal: Think of a happy memory.

633
01:17:25.670 --> 01:17:34.009
Dr. Karan Mittal: With your eyes closed, think of a happy memory, maybe the most happiest, or maybe the happiest memory that you can think of today.

634
01:17:43.620 --> 01:17:50.130
Dr. Karan Mittal: And as you bring that memory to… bring that memory to your consciousness, just be aware of your body.

635
01:17:50.470 --> 01:17:52.520
Dr. Karan Mittal: Where do you feel that happiness?

636
01:18:07.530 --> 01:18:15.869
Dr. Karan Mittal: Just go into that memory as vividly as possible, as live as possible, and then see where did you feel that happiness in your body?

637
01:18:35.600 --> 01:18:41.020
Dr. Karan Mittal: And again, I want you to move to another memory, probably a negative memory, a sad memory.

638
01:18:41.330 --> 01:18:43.800
Dr. Karan Mittal: And see, where do you locate that sadness in your world.

639
01:19:05.990 --> 01:19:24.790
Dr. Karan Mittal: And if you're done, you can open your eyes. We'll go into a deeper version of the exercise in one of the future sessions on how to work with these memories. But… but I want you to come up with how did you feel? Like, just the three names, like, where did you feel your mind, your happiness, and your… probably the negative emotion? Any one of you could share, probably.

640
01:19:25.170 --> 01:19:26.929
Dr. Karan Mittal: If at all you felt it.

